  "lessons": [
    {
      "key": "lesson-1",
      "name": "What is Intelligence?",
      "absolute_position": 1,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "overview": "**What does it mean to be intelligent?**\n\nIn this lesson, students explore what intelligence means, examining the question from a human and machine perspective. They begin with their own intuitions and, through engaging with thought experiments and classroom discussions, they refine their thinking and emerge with a clearer understanding of their own definition of intelligence.",
        "preparation": "- Print copies of the Logic-Based AI Unit Guide (one for each student)\n- Print and cut out copies of the Intelligence Card Sort activity (one for each pair of two students)",
        "student_overview": "**What does it mean to be intelligent?**\n\nExplore what intelligence means, examining the question from a human and machine perspective."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
